+### §check-fails-open — a failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit
+- Since: 2026-10-23 (user overrode the 2026-09-11 decision)
+- Decision: `set -euo pipefail`. Any failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit. Large staged files are still
+  only warned about; the script exits 0 when nothing fails.
+- Forbidden: dropping `-e`, or swallowing a command failure so the check exits 0 after an internal error.
+- Reason: the maintainer chose on 2026-10-23 to override the earlier fail-open decision, so that internal failures are
+  surfaced instead of silently passing.
+- History: the 2026-09-11 decision forbade `set -e` because a `wc` failure on a staged-then-deleted file aborted the
+  check and blocked every commit in the repository for a day (2026-09-10). That risk is accepted by the override;
+  the `[ -f "$f" ] || continue` guard still skips deleted files.
